Testing list clear (nadiifi) method:
1. Basic usage:
  Original list: [A, B, C]
  After nadiifi(): []
2. Clearing an already empty list:
  Empty list: []
  After nadiifi(): []
3. Clearing a list with nested elements:
  Complex list: [[1, 2], [3, 4], 5, text]
  After nadiifi(): []
4. Adding items to a cleared list:
  Original list: [10, 20, 30]
  After nadiifi(): []
  After adding new items: [40, 50]
5. Chaining operations with nadiifi():
  Original list: [1, 2, 3]
  After: chain.nadiifi().kudar(4).kudar(5): [4, 5]
The nadiifi() method successfully clears all items from a list.
